module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Immersion.ClosedSubspaceScheme

/-!
# The ideal sheaf of a closed immersion into a scheme is quasi-coherent

Let `X` be a scheme and `i : Z ⟶ X` a closed immersion of locally ringed spaces. The kernel of
`𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_Z` is a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. Conversely, a sheaf of ideals on `X` is
quasi-coherent exactly when it is locally generated by sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isQuasicoherent_idealSheaf`: the ideal sheaf of a closed immersion of
  locally ringed spaces into a scheme is quasi-coherent.
* `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isQuasicoherent_iff_localGenerators`: a sheaf of ideals on a scheme is
  quasi-coherent if and only if it is locally generated by sections.

## Implementation notes

Both statements reduce to the case of a morphism of schemes. The source `Z` of the closed
immersion is a scheme by `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.sourceScheme`, so `i` is a morphism of schemes
by `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.sourceSchemeHom`; the sixth condition of the characterization
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersionTFAE.closedImmersion_tfae` is the ringed-space
closed-immersion hypothesis, from which the first — Mathlib's closed-immersion predicate for
schemes — follows, and then
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersionTFAE.isQuasicoherent_idealSheaf` applies.

For the characterization of quasi-coherent ideal sheaves, one direction is the local generators
extracted from the quasi-coherent datum. For the other, a locally generated sheaf of ideals cuts
out a closed subspace of `X` ([Stacks, Tag 01HN]) whose ideal sheaf is canonically the given
one, so the first statement transports along that identification.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01HN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01HN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01IN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01QO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01QO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.ClosedImmersion

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01IN.** The kernel of `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_Z` for a closed immersion of
locally ringed spaces `i : Z ⟶ X` into a scheme is a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. -/
@[stacks 01IN "kernel_quasi_coherent"]
theorem isQuasicoherent_idealSheaf (X : Scheme.{u}) (Z : LocallyRingedSpace.{u})
    (i : Z ⟶ X.toLocallyRingedSpace) [hi : IsClosedImmersion i.toShHom] :
    (idealSheaf i.toShHom).IsQuasicoherent := by
  have hi' : IsClosedImmersion (sourceSchemeHom X Z i).toLRSHom.toShHom := hi
  have hci : AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion (sourceSchemeHom X Z i) :=
    ((Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersionTFAE.closedImmersion_tfae
      (sourceSchemeHom X Z i)).out 6 1).mp hi'
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ClosedImmersionTFAE.isQuasicoherent_idealSheaf
    (sourceSchemeHom X Z i)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01IN.** A sheaf of ideals on a scheme is locally generated by sections
if and only if it is quasi-coherent. -/
@[stacks 01IN "ideal_quasi_coherent_iff_locally_generated"]
theorem isQuasicoherent_iff_localGenerators (X : Scheme.{u})
    (J : (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf).Submodule) :
    J.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent ↔
      Nonempty (SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData.{u} J.toSheafOfModules) := by
  refine ⟨fun hJ ↦ ⟨hJ.nonempty_quasicoherentData.some.localGeneratorsData⟩, fun hJ ↦ ?_⟩
  let j : J.toSheafOfModules ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf := J.ι
  let m : Mono j := inferInstance
  let D := @closedSubspace X.toLocallyRingedSpace J.toSheafOfModules j m hJ
  exact CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_of_iso
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (structureSheafRing X.toLocallyRingedSpace.toRingedSpace))
    (@ClosedSubspaceData.idealIso X.toLocallyRingedSpace J.toSheafOfModules j m D).symm
    (@isQuasicoherent_idealSheaf X
      (@ClosedSubspaceData.space X.toLocallyRingedSpace J.toSheafOfModules j m D)
      (@ClosedSubspaceData.inclusion X.toLocallyRingedSpace J.toSheafOfModules j m D)
      (@ClosedSubspaceData.isClosedImmersion X.toLocallyRingedSpace J.toSheafOfModules j m D))

end Stacks.ClosedImmersion

end
